@feat-jarvis-006 @nats-chat-gateway @fleet-surface
Feature: NATS Chat Gateway
  As Rich (via the Open WebUI pipe and any other NATS-aware adapter)
  I want Jarvis to accept chat requests over the fleet bus and reply on
  the same bus, exactly as the CLI REPL accepts them over stdin today
  So that the Open WebUI pipe and any future fleet member can hold a
  conversation with the supervisor — including its dispatch and
  queue-build tool calls — without the supervisor's reasoning, session,
  or fleet-registration paths having to know which surface is talking
  to it

  Background:
    Given Jarvis has been booted with a connected NATS transport
    And Jarvis is registered on the fleet under the identifier "jarvis"
    And Jarvis's heartbeat is publishing on the fleet heartbeat subject
    And Jarvis is listening for chat requests on the jarvis command subject
    And the supervisor, session manager, and dispatch tools are wired

  # ─── GROUP A: Key Examples ──────────────────────────────────────────────

  # Why: The bootstrap criterion — the command surface exists at all
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] Implementation shape — the chat gateway ADDS only the agents.command.jarvis subscription and in-flight drain bookkeeping to the existing AppState.nats_client; it does not clone a full NATSAdapter because build_app_state already owns connect, register, heartbeat, deregister, disconnect
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] Subscription uses subscribe-with-reply on the flat subject agents.command.jarvis exactly (Bug #1 and Bug #4 must-replicate from the scope doc)
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Starting the chat gateway subscribes Jarvis to the jarvis command subject
    Given Jarvis has just started in chat-gateway mode
    When the chat gateway finishes its startup sequence
    Then Jarvis should be subscribed to the jarvis command subject
    And Jarvis should be ready to receive chat requests from the fleet

  # Why: Core happy path — the OpenWebUI pipe's primary use case
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] Single command verb — the chat gateway accepts the literal command string "chat" and no other verbs
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: A chat request is answered by the supervisor on the reply inbox
    Given Rich sends a chat request through the fleet asking Jarvis a question
    When Jarvis receives the chat request
    Then the supervisor should be asked to answer the question
    And the supervisor's reply should be delivered on the requester's reply inbox
    And the reply should carry the supervisor's response text
    And the reply should carry the same correlation identifier as the request

  # Why: Bug #1 — observers that watch the canonical result topic must also see the answer
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] Dual-publish — every chat reply is delivered on BOTH the requester's reply inbox (raw bytes) AND the canonical result topic agents.result.jarvis (envelope-wrapped)
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: A chat reply is also published on the canonical Jarvis result topic
    Given Rich sends a chat request through the fleet
    When the supervisor's reply is ready
    Then a result envelope should also be published on Jarvis's canonical result topic
    And the canonical result envelope should identify Jarvis as the source
    And the canonical result envelope should carry the same correlation identifier as the request

  # Why: Proves the gateway routes through the supervisor's full tool surface, not just echo
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] Result payload shape — the reply carries the supervisor's response text, the list of tools the supervisor called, and the originating correlation identifier
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: A chat request that triggers a fleet dispatch returns the specialist's answer
    Given Rich sends a chat request that asks Jarvis to consult a specialist agent
    And the named specialist is available on the fleet
    When Jarvis receives the chat request
    Then the supervisor should call dispatch-by-capability against the specialist
    And the specialist's answer should be folded into the reply Rich receives
    And the reply should record that the dispatch tool was called

  # Why: Proves the gateway routes through queue-build too — closes the FEAT-005 loop over NATS
  @key-example
  Scenario: A chat request that asks Jarvis to queue a build returns the queued acknowledgement
    Given Rich sends a chat request asking Jarvis to queue a build for a planned feature
    When Jarvis receives the chat request
    Then the supervisor should call queue-build for that feature
    And the reply should tell Rich the build has been queued
    And the reply should record that the queue-build tool was called

  # Why: Multi-turn conversation — proves the gateway preserves session context across requests
  @key-example
  Scenario: A follow-up chat request on the same conversation sees the earlier turn
    Given Rich has already sent one chat request to Jarvis through the fleet
    When Rich sends a second chat request that refers back to the first
    Then the supervisor's reply should reflect the context of the earlier turn
    And both replies should be associated with the same Jarvis chat session

  # ─── GROUP B: Boundary Conditions ───────────────────────────────────────

  # Why: Just-inside drain — an in-flight chat that finishes within the drain window is delivered
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] Drain timeout is 30 seconds, matching the study-tutor NATSAdapter template
  @boundary
  Scenario: A chat reply that completes within the drain window is delivered before shutdown
    Given Rich's chat request is being answered when Jarvis is asked to shut down
    And the supervisor finishes its answer within the drain window
    When the chat gateway drains in-flight requests
    Then Rich should still receive the supervisor's reply
    And the drain should complete without warning

  # Why: Just-outside drain — an in-flight chat that overshoots the drain window does not block shutdown
  @boundary @edge-case
  Scenario: A chat reply that overshoots the drain window does not block shutdown
    Given Rich's chat request is still being answered when Jarvis is asked to shut down
    And the supervisor has not finished its answer when the drain window expires
