  # ─── GROUP D: Edge Cases ────────────────────────────────────────────────

  # Why: SIGINT during a long-running chat is the most common operator action — must drain cleanly
  @edge-case @smoke
  Scenario: Interrupt-while-busy drains the in-flight chat and deregisters from the fleet
    Given Rich's chat request is being answered when the operator interrupts the chat gateway
    When the chat gateway shuts down
    Then the in-flight chat should be allowed to finish within the drain window
    And Rich should receive the supervisor's reply if it finished in time
    And the chat gateway should deregister Jarvis from the fleet before disconnecting

  # Why: Two near-simultaneous chats from the same surface must both reach the supervisor
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Two concurrent chat requests are both answered
    Given Rich sends two chat requests in close succession
