  # ─── Security ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  # Why: Source-id discipline — Jarvis must not be tricked into answering an unsigned request
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] A request whose envelope source_id is empty or not registered on the fleet is answered with a refused reply rather than silently dropped, so the requester is told to retry from a registered surface
  @edge-case @security
  Scenario: A chat request whose envelope source_id is unrecognised is refused
    Given a chat request arrives on the Jarvis command subject
    But the request's envelope does not identify a known fleet member as its source
    When Jarvis evaluates the request
    Then Jarvis should reply that the request was not accepted
    And the reply should indicate the request did not succeed
